  "id": "Compound::DB01274 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Arformoterol is shown to interact with Cyp2c19 through a series of mechanistic pathways involving the enzyme Cyp2d6 and Cyp2c9. The evidence suggests that Arformoterol binds to Cyp2d6, which then participates in the arachidonic acid epoxygenase activity, ultimately leading to Cyp2c19 being involved in this process. Similarly, Arformoterol binds to Cyp2c9, which also participates in the arachidonic acid epoxygenase activity, and this pathway ultimately leads to Cyp2c19 being involved. These findings indicate a potential mechanism by which Arformoterol may influence Cyp2c19 activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The consistent binding of Arformoterol to Cyp2d6 and Cyp2c9, along with their shared participation in arachidonic acid epoxygenase activity, supports a plausible pathway linking Arformoterol to Cyp2c19. The evidence is robust and aligns with the expected biological roles of these enzymes, suggesting a mechanistic basis for the observed interactions.",
